{
  "version": "airport-sides.v1",
  "checkedOn": "2026-09-29",
  "notes": [
    "Hall sides: the airport's own facility location text names each departure hall with its terminal side (quoted in evidence). The owner's reading of the official accessibility maps (https://www.airport.kr/ap_ko/908/subview.do) gives the same split: T1 1-3 east / 4-6 west (axis between halls 3 and 4, G/H check-in), T2 2 east / 1 west (axis between halls 1 and 2, F/G check-in).",
    "The T2 texts ('1번 출국장 서편', '2번 출국장 동편') could also be read as a side within the hall; they agree with the owner's map reading, which is the basis used here.",
    "A5 fields: data.go.kr 15095066 lists the items as T1 출국장1..6, 출국장 합계, T2 출국장1, 2, 합계; the V5.0 field names are t1dg1..t1dg6, t1dgsum1, t2dg1, t2dg2, t2dgsum2 (docs/DATA_SOURCES.md). Production (run 36518271601) showed the official aggregate equal to the sum of the six (T1) and two (T2) hall fields in all 96 hour bands checked; t1dg5 and t1dg6 are separate fields, never a combined one.",
    "Gate sides are listed only where official text names the gate together with 동편/서편/중앙. Every other gate is 'UNVERIFIED': no range is filled in from gate numbers, and no side is inferred from an airline.",
    "The published gate ranges are 1-50 (T1), 101-132 (탑승동) and 208-290 (T2) (https://www.airport.kr/ap_ko/886/subview.do). A T2 '1번 게이트' in the facility text is an entrance, not a boarding gate, and is not used.",
    "The 탑승동 (Concourse) is its own building; its east/west gates are never counted as T1 east/west."
  ],
